  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARM: Demographic Resilience: Expanding Women&apos;s Capacities and Choices through Data-driven Policies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to enhance Armenia&#x2019;s demographic resilience and economic growth by empowering women through lifelong education, gender-responsive policy-making, and evidence-based strategies to address gender disparities in the labor market and beyond.
Through collaboration with key stakeholders including the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs, Ministry of Education, Science, Culture and Sports, Yerevan State University, United Social Services and the Armenian National Statistical Committee, as well as civil society organizations, this project will utilize innovative methodologies such as National Time Transfer Accounts (NTTA) to provide critical insights into gendered labor dynamics. A key component of this initiative is the support to development of a Demographic Center within Yerevan State University, which will drive research, policy analysis, and data collection. Additionally, the project will strengthen Armenia&#x2019;s national data management capacity to support evidence-based policy development that strengthens gender-responsive demographic resilience. In its pilot phase, the project will implement a component focused on lifelong learning, supporting women&#x2019;s (re)entry into the labour market, and enhancing their knowledge and skills. In all, the project thus will have a sustainable impact on policy making, capacity building of state systems and infrastructure and paving a way for greater empowerment for women</narrative>
  </description>
